<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Auto Backup rules for API 26-30 (API 31+ uses data_extraction_rules.xml).

  Only the Room database goes to the cloud: titles, reading positions, speed
  and the per-book original/cover pointers. That is the part that actually
  hurts to lose and it measures in kilobytes.

  files/books (extracted text, covers, and the preserved PDF/EPUB originals) is
  deliberately left out. Auto Backup enforces a per-app quota, and a single
  preserved original can exceed it on its own — at which point the WHOLE backup
  silently fails and even the progress stops being saved. Excluding the bulk is
  what makes the small, valuable part reliable.

  Naming any <include> makes everything else excluded by default, so the play
  flavour's cached billing entitlement stays out too. That is intended: it is
  re-queried from Play on launch and should never ride along to another account.

  The -wal/-shm side files travel with the database on purpose. Room runs in WAL
  mode, so the .db alone can be a stale snapshot with recent writes still in the
  log; backing up the set together keeps it consistent.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="database" path="rapid_reader.db" />
    <include domain="database" path="rapid_reader.db-wal" />
    <include domain="database" path="rapid_reader.db-shm" />
</full-backup-content>
